### Jira Summary
Add CloudWatch Alarm for Missing Jenkins Controller Logs

### Description
Implemented CloudWatch heartbeat monitoring to detect interruptions in log delivery from the Jenkins controller to AWS CloudWatch.

### Changes Implemented
- Configured the Jenkins controller to generate heartbeat logs every minute.
- Updated the CloudWatch Agent to collect and forward heartbeat logs.
- Created a CloudWatch metric filter to track incoming heartbeat events.
- Added a CloudWatch alarm that triggers when no heartbeat is received for five consecutive minutes.
- Integrated the alarm with the existing Jenkins SNS notification topic to send alerts when log delivery stops and recovery notifications when it resumes.
- Preserved existing Jenkins monitoring and alerting configurations.

### Validation
- Terraform plan completed successfully.
- Confirmed the plan includes the new CloudWatch metric filter and missing-logs alarm.
- CloudWatch log delivery and SNS notification testing remain to be verified after deployment.

### Expected Outcome
The monitoring solution provides automated notification when the Jenkins heartbeat log delivery pipeline stops functioning, improving visibility into CloudWatch Agent and log forwarding failures.
